#: ../../source/components_basic/11-component_raindrop.rst:25
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/components_basic/11-component_raindrop.rst:27
msgid "A raindrop sensor, or raindrop detection sensor, is used to detect whether it is raining and also the rainfall. It is widely used in the automatic wiper system, smart lighting system and sunroof system of automobiles."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/components_basic/11-component_raindrop.rst:30
msgid "Principle"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/components_basic/11-component_raindrop.rst:32
msgid "Raindrop sensor is basically a board on which nickel is coated in the form of lines. It works on the principal of resistance. When there is no rain drop on board. Resistance is high so we gets high voltage according to V=IR. When rain drop present it reduces the resistance because water is conductor of electricity and presence of water connects nickel lines in parallel so reduced resistance and reduced voltage drop across it. The more intense the rainfall the lower the resistance."
msgstr ""

