#: ../../source/components_basic/11-component_raindrop.rst:86
msgid "Here, a constant integer named ``sensorPin`` is defined and assigned the value 7. This corresponds to the digital pin on the Arduino board where the raindrops detection sensor is connected."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/components_basic/11-component_raindrop.rst:92
msgid "Setting up the pin mode and initiating serial communication"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/components_basic/11-component_raindrop.rst:94
msgid "In the ``setup()`` function, two essential steps are performed. Firstly, ``pinMode()`` is used to set the ``sensorPin`` as an input, enabling us to read digital values from the raindrops sensor. Secondly, serial communication is initialized with a baud rate of 9600."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/components_basic/11-component_raindrop.rst:103
msgid "Reading the digital value and sending it to the serial monitor."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/components_basic/11-component_raindrop.rst:105
msgid "The ``loop()`` function reads the digital value from the raindrops sensor using ``digitalRead()``. This value (either HIGH or LOW) is printed to the Serial Monitor. The program then waits for 50 milliseconds before the next reading."
msgstr ""

